  "owner": "Fictional example product owner",
  "audience": "Product owners and delivery teams reviewing a fictional prototype",
  "goal": "Compare several views of one form while editing repeated line items directly in its table.",
  "scope": "One request form, three list views and one repeated table (1–8 items). Lists show whole requests, not flattened child rows. No approval engine or role enforcement.",
  "theme": "bootstrap",
  "languages": ["de", "en"],
  "decisions": "All lists share requests and their repeated items. New requests has a fixed status preset; Overview disables modifications for every viewer. Planned later roles: requester prepares requests; purchasing processes them; observer reads overviews. A view preset is not row-level access control.",
  "questions": "Which fields become read-only after submission? May requesters edit only their own records, and how will ownership be established? Who may change status or remove repeated positions? These policies are not enforced by this prototype.",
